---
title: "Shell completion"
---

*Reference: [CLI](cli.tmd) · Shell completion · [Front matter](frontmatter.tmd) · [Cell options](cell-options.tmd) · [Configuration](configuration.tmd) · [Shortcodes](shortcodes.tmd) · [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.tmd)*

Tab completion for the `taliesin` (and `tali`) command. Press Tab and it offers
subcommands, flags, and, for a path argument, only `.tmd` files plus directories that
contain one, with site and book roots listed first. Directories with no `.tmd` inside
(and build folders like `target/`) are hidden, so finding the document, deck, or site
you want to open is quick.

All the logic lives in the binary, so every shell stays in sync and there is nothing to
keep updated by hand. Install the script for your shell once:

- **bash:** `taliesin completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/taliesin`
- **zsh:** `taliesin completions zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_taliesin"`, then run `compinit`
- **fish:** `taliesin completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/taliesin.fish`
- **PowerShell:** `taliesin completions powershell >> $PROFILE`

Open a new shell (for zsh, re-run `compinit`) and press Tab after `tali preview`. The
same completion also drives `taliesin build`, `render`, `check`, and the other
path-taking commands.
